course: dictionary
lesson: 6512
title: Neighbors: people, numbers and spelling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A neighbor is a person who lives next to you or near you. «Our neighbor always waves when we walk past her house.» The clue is in the words around it: she lives close by, so she is a neighbor, not a stranger.
explain: The word also means a person or thing that is next to another one. In maths, a number's neighbors are the numbers just before and after it: the neighbors of 7 are 6 and 8. To check, swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: The spelling depends on where you are. British English writes «neighbour» with ei and an -our ending, while American English writes «neighbor». Both spellings mean the same thing, so you just need to know which one your text uses.
fact: A neighbor is a person who lives next to you or near you.
fact: In maths, the neighbors of a number are the numbers just before and after it: the neighbors of 7 are 6 and 8.
fact: «Neighbour» is the British spelling; American English writes «neighbor».
fact: Studio Ghibli, a Japanese studio co-founded by Hayao Miyazaki, is famous for hand-drawn films such as «My Neighbor Totoro».
fact: «Spirited Away» is a Studio Ghibli film that won an Oscar.
exercise: The neighbors of 7 are which two numbers? | 5 and 7 | 1 and 7 | 7 and 9 | *6 and 8
exercise: «Our neighbor always waves when we walk past her house.» Who is the neighbor in this sentence? | The postman | A number on the page | *The person who lives next door | A tree on the hill
exercise: A person who lives next door to you is called a what? | *A neighbor | A pupil | A cousin | A stranger
test: In maths, what are the neighbors of 12? | *11 and 13 | 10 and 12 | 1 and 2 | 12 and 14
test: According to the text, which Studio Ghibli film won an Oscar? | My Neighbor Totoro | Hayao Miyazaki | *Spirited Away | Studio Ghibli
exam: Which spelling is the American one? | *neighbor | neighbour | nabor | neighbur
